[h2]Battle Royale[/h2]
Play solo, in duos or in squads of four. The match starts with a transport flight. Follow the route on the map and pick where to jump. The lobby can let teammates jump together. Loot buildings and move into each new circle. The last surviving player or team wins.

[h2]What to look for[/h2]
[list]
[*]The current circle, the next circle and the time until the zone moves are shown on the map and HUD. The later circles close faster and do more damage outside the zone.
[*]Loot depends on the terrain and building type. Helmets and vests show armor levels in the inventory. Uniforms, vests and backpacks show storage space.
[*]Double-click medical supplies in your inventory. Bandages heal 10 HP up to 75% health. First-aid kits also stop at 75%, medikits heal to full, and energy drinks heal over time. Moving or firing can interrupt treatment.
[*]Ground vehicles, boats, helicopters and airfield aircraft can spawn, depending on the terrain and vehicle setting. Supply drops are optional.
[/list]

[h2]Teams and AI[/h2]
In duos and squads, players can crawl while downed. A teammate can stabilize and revive them. If nobody on the team is left standing, the team is eliminated. Solo players are eliminated immediately on death.
With AI fill on, AI can fill team slots. Bots parachute in, loot, heal, use vehicles and move to the circle. The lobby can pick a fixed player-plus-AI count or scale it by terrain, up to 150.

[h2]Lobby parameters[/h2]
Team size, AI fill and skill, combatant count, warmup, team jumps, zone speed, loot, vehicles, supply drops, weather, start time, time multipliers and third-person view. After elimination you can spectate. The end screen shows the match results.

[h2]Start the scenario[/h2]
Host the scenario in multiplayer and open Parameters in the lobby. The Chernarus 2020 edition requires the CUP addons listed on that Workshop page.

